Phil,

Great piece of retro work!  I first worked on the a KA10 with a DEC 340
scope at Ohio State in 1970.  We wrote a lot of assembler to drive the scope
but not much has survived.  It always had a lot of flicker, which i quite
miss!  It had a light pen also. we wrote a software character generator ( we
didn't have hardware characters) and we wrote a on screen editor which most
people thought was a waste of resources (how time changes things) i have a
hardcopy of it but it would be a lot of work to bring it up.  it is in pdp10
assembler and a flock of binary IOWds.

the life game we build has dissapeared.

good luck with the simulator extensions.  i had a idea to build a "modern"
vector scope using a display from an old atari asteriods game and a small
micro which would eat up pdp10 io words for the 340, but i have a business
to run and fun comes last.

gerry
