Alan Frisbie wrote:
> I have a real DEC VS60 (GT48) in my home for Lunar Lander, etc.,

Oo, let me know if you need help aligning or programming it.

In the late 1970s I was chief systems analyst and lead
programmer for a small company whose product was based on
the VS60, and I worked with its designer in DEC's Marlboro
facility.  Despite the reduced bandwidth due to the
principal customer insisting on the video drivers being
located below the display instead of packed around it, it
was a very nice interface (we used Talos digitizing tablet
with a stylus, via DR11-C, in place of the light pen).
RT-11 had nice support for both the VT11 and the VS60 (LK40
keyboard) as console display, and TECO in screen mode on
that display was the nicest editing environment available.

If you ever want to get rid of your VS60 I can provide it
with a nice caring home!

When I get enough time (probably after October) I'd be
happy to review the VT11 piece of SIMH and add VS60 support.



