"H Vlems" <hvlems.nieuw@zonnet.nl> wrote:
> That was the TU56 IIRC. The TU58 is a block structured tape and supports
> random access like a disk.

TU56 and TU58 are both block-structured.  TU56 is the original DECtape,
which used 3/4-inch open-reel tape on roughly 4-inch spools.  TU58 is
DECtape II which uses DC100 cartridges.  Note that TU58 cartridges came
preformatted, and the drive is NOT capable of reformatting them, so if
a TU58 cartridge has been reused in another vendor's DC100 drive, it will
no longer be usable as a TU58.

The drive that used the audio cassette (Philips Compact Cassette) was
the TU60.


