There are two versions of the PWS, the Miata and and the Miata GL.  The 
Miata GL has SCSI on the motherboard where as the earlier version does 
not. The Miata GL will boot from the IDE CDRom. The earlier Miata's IDE 
CDrom will NOT boot.
You most probably have the earlier version, so you will need a SCSI 
CDRom to boot to OpenVMS.  It is highly recommended that you add a 
second SCSI card to put the CDRom on, rather than just add it to the 
existing SCSI bus.  If you add to the existing SCSI bus, the slowest 
device will set the speed of data transfer for the entire bus.  The 
CDRom is a VERY slow device.  The performance hit is very noticeable.

TomC

