I found these while going through my basement in preparation for moving, and
thought it might be of great interest to DEC collectors.

http://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&category=208&item=3626709619

A little background on these cards:

The Compaq "merger" was the biggest shock in my Digital life.  I was on my
way to the local DEC office, when one of my customers called me on the cell
phone and said "How does it feel to work for Compaq?  "Of course he is
kidding," I thought.  "How could the small fish swallow the big one?"  There
had been no hint of a merger.  Sure we were struggling a bit in recent
years, as KO bowed out and Bob Palmer took ther reigns, but I had no idea
that the whole company was on the block.  After a minute of talking, I
realized he wasn't kidding.  When I arrived at the office, the rumor was
confirmed.  We were all in shock.

I imagine that scenario was pretty common with about 89,998 other people
around the world.  Maybe some of you were in that count.  The Digital pride
was still alive, although being muffled by the Compaq way of doing things.
Digital letterhead and envelopes were the first to get tossed.  Nothing
Digital could remain.  Somehow, though, the Digital Press was able to
produce these playing cards before being shut down.  Someone remaining in
upper management had the inspiration to distribute these to the "pre-merger
Digital" employees.  I think it must have been a labor of love that went
into producing these momentos for DEC employees to commemorate the greatness
of their 40-year history.  This was the last hurrah. . .




