If what I understand is correct, you have:
1. SCSI disk drive with no case, that is inteded to be internal to some 
device (VS 3100 in htis case).
2. a situation where when you connect the drive to the interal supply,
the supply shuts down.
3. what you have not told us is what the drive type is or the current, 
or the config of the VS3100.  Each board eats up some amount of power, so...
You could have either a "weak" power supply OR
a dis drive that is bad or
a disk drive that is too power hungry for your system even if the PS is 
not weak.

I have had drive die, main bearing on the motor, and have it kill a 
power supply.
I have had disk drives that brought the power budget beyond what the 
system could support.

You can look for an external drive case, with a hefty supply, and 
connect it to the Vs3100.
You can acquire a new drive with better (lower) power consumption numbers.

I hope this helps
bob
