Here's an update of what I found out so far:

First, i checked the wiring/voltages on the power connectors, since the
swapped wires problem was brought to my attention by a number of people
(thanks you so much guys -- you are incredible!).

So, after (quite) a while of searching I found a very old analogous
Volt/Ampere-meter, my dad one gave me -- one you would use for mere
testing of batteries... So maybe I shouldn't put much trust on the
accuracy of this old gadget, given its age (really looks worn)...

On the (female) main plug that comes out of the PSU I'd find the
following:
______
\4321/
 ----
 
4: red, +9V (!)
3: black, GND (no voltage against 3)
2: black, GND (no voltage against 2)
1: orange, +>15V (needle whacks against the top of analogous 15V scale.)

