> Randy Park <rjpark@mindspring.nospaam.com> wrote:
> >   VaxStations 3100/30
>
> Any SCSI disk <=1GB should do. Beware! 3100/20-76 have a bug that prevent
> them from booting larger than 1GB disks under VMS. I forget what exactly
> it is, but some logical wrap-around causes the boot loader to hickup.
>
> There is always the HP parts exchange, but that tends to be expensive for
> disks (not so for KGPSA, though, I was positively surprised).
>
It is not a matter of a bug but rather a design limitation in the boot rom's
in the 3100's that is causing this problem. The system will boot but if one
or more parts of the bootstrap software happen to live above the 1 GB limit
then VMB cannot locate the software. As long as you are sure all relevant
VMS software lives below 1 GB then a 3100 will happily boot from a 4 GB
disk.

Hans



